.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-ACCEPT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-accept - Accept an invitation bound to this account


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team accept <invitation> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Accept an invitation addressed to this account and join the team. Find the invitation ID
with pb team invitations. The command prints the team as it is after you joined.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for accept

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb team invitations
  pb team accept inv_abc123
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
